---
import QuestIcon from '../components/QuestIcon.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/data';

const topics = [
  { id: 'questbook', title: 'Quest book' },
  { id: 'first-steps', title: 'Wood & shelter' },
  { id: 'factory', title: 'Andesite & clay' },
  { id: 'appraisal', title: 'Identify gear' },
  { id: 'skills', title: 'Levels & skills' },
  { id: 'combat', title: 'Combat' },
];
const spruce = href('media/textures/spruce-planks.png');
const earlyMaterials = [
  {
    name: 'Andesite',
    image: 'media/ponder/textures/minecraft/block/andesite.png',
    description: 'Mine the speckled gray patches in exposed stone. Check hillsides and shallow caves, and bring a pickaxe.',
  },
  {
    name: 'Clay',
    image: 'media/ponder/textures/minecraft/block/clay.png',
    description: 'Look for smooth blue-gray blocks on riverbeds and in shallow water. Dig them with a shovel and keep the clay balls loose.',
  },
];
---

<Layout title="Getting started" description="Open the quest book, gather wood, andesite and clay, identify your first piece of gear and learn how character levels work.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Handbook / Basics</p>
  <h1>Getting started</h1>
  <p class="intro">Follow your first quests, gather what you need for Create, and turn dungeon finds into gear you can use.</p>

  <nav class="guide-jumps" aria-label="Getting started sections">
    {topics.map(({ id, title }) => <a href={'#' + id}>{title}</a>)}
  </nav>

  <div class="guide-topics" style={{ '--guide-spruce': `url("${spruce}")` }}>
    <section class="guide-topic" id="questbook" aria-labelledby="questbook-title">
      <header class="guide-heading">
        <QuestIcon name="bookopen" size={28} />
        <h2 id="questbook-title">Open the quest book</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="guide-body">
        <ol>
          <li>Open your inventory with <kbd>E</kbd> by default. Click the <strong>Quest Book</strong> icon in the upper-left corner.</li>
          <li>Open <strong>Town Square → The Story</strong> and complete <strong>A New Beginning</strong>. Then look under <strong>Forging Ahead</strong> for <strong>Chapter I | Getting Started</strong>.</li>
          <li>Open completed quests to claim their rewards. To set a shortcut, find <strong>Open Quests</strong> under <strong>FTB Quests</strong> in <strong>Options → Controls → Key Binds</strong>.</li>
        </ol>
        <figure class="guide-figure">
          <img src={href('media/tutorial/quest-book-orientation.webp')} width="840" height="226" decoding="async" alt="The purple Quest Book icon and the Story, Chapters and Market sections." />
        </figure>
        <p><a href={href('guides/tutorial/')}>Open the full in-game tutorial</a> for chapter milestones, claims and travel.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-topic" id="first-steps" aria-labelledby="first-steps-title">
      <header class="guide-heading">
        <QuestIcon name="lantern" size={28} />
        <h2 id="first-steps-title">Chop wood and set up camp</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="guide-body">
        <p>Hold left click on a tree trunk to break your first logs by hand. Turn some into planks, sticks and a crafting table. Make a wooden pickaxe, mine cobblestone for a stone axe, and gather food before heading farther out.</p>
        <figure class="guide-figure">
          <img src={href('media/tutorial/chopping-wood.webp')} width="1600" height="804" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="A stone axe strikes an oak log, with cracks spreading across the bark." />
          <figcaption>Keep a few whole logs. Right-click one with an axe to strip it, then apply Andesite Alloy to make a Create Andesite Casing.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-topic" id="factory" aria-labelledby="factory-title">
      <header class="guide-heading">
        <QuestIcon name="pickaxe" size={28} />
        <h2 id="factory-title">Gather andesite and clay</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="guide-body">
        <div class="material-grid">
          {earlyMaterials.map(({ name, image, description }) => (
            <div class="material">
              <img src={href(image)} alt="" width="48" height="48" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
              <div><h3>{name}</h3><p>{description}</p></div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p>Arrange <strong>2 Andesite</strong> and <strong>2 Clay Balls</strong> in a 2 × 2 checkerboard to craft <strong>1 Andesite Alloy</strong>. Stock up on both for your first Makeshift Mechanisms and Andesite Machine.</p>
        <p>Hover over an item in JEI and press <kbd>R</kbd> for its recipes or <kbd>U</kbd> for its uses. Follow <a href={href('chapters/')}>Chapters I and II</a> for the first machines, or browse the <a id="workshop-builds" href={href('tutorials/')}>workshop build guides</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-topic" id="appraisal" aria-labelledby="appraisal-title">
      <header class="guide-heading">
        <QuestIcon name="satchel" size={28} />
        <h2 id="appraisal-title">Build your first Identifier</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="guide-body">
        <div class="identifier-layout">
          <div>
            <p>Make an <strong>Identifier</strong> early so you can use the gear you find while exploring. At a crafting table, put <strong>2 emeralds</strong> in the top corners and <strong>1 book</strong> in the center. Fill the six other slots with <strong>iron ingots</strong>.</p>
            <ol>
              <li>Place the Identifier, right-click it and put an <strong>unidentified equipment token</strong> in the tray.</li>
              <li>Check the <strong>vanilla XP</strong> cost, confirm and collect the revealed gear.</li>
              <li>Compare the stats and affixes before equipping or salvaging it.</li>
            </ol>
            <p>See <a href={href('loot/')}>Loot &amp; Appraisal</a> for loot sources, salvage and the Mechanical Identifier.</p>
          </div>
          <img src={href('media/tutorial/manual-identifier.png')} width="144" height="144" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The manual Identifier block, with a gold-trimmed crafting grid on top." />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-topic" id="skills" aria-labelledby="skills-title">
      <header class="guide-heading">
        <QuestIcon name="skill_point" size={28} />
        <h2 id="skills-title">Read levels and spend skill points</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="guide-body">
        <figure class="guide-figure">
          <img src={href('media/tutorial/character-level.webp')} width="1440" height="810" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="A level 4 badge next to the name above Mikaaah’s Minecraft character." />
          <figcaption>Illustration of Mikaaah’s player nameplate at character level 4.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Character XP</strong> comes from activities such as fighting, mining natural blocks, farming, fishing and exploring. Level up to earn skill points. You start with a level cap of 10.</li>
          <li><strong>Vanilla XP</strong> is the green experience bar. You spend it at the Identifier and on enchanting.</li>
          <li><strong>Open Character</strong> with <kbd>I</kbd> by default or click your portrait in the survival inventory. Check your progress, choose an Origin and spend points in the skill tree.</li>
          <li><strong>Enemy levels</strong> appear above scaled mobs. Higher levels can mean more health and harder hits. Check the badge before you get into melee range.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>See <a href={href('mechanics/#leveling')}>Levels &amp; Origins</a> for XP and level caps, or try a route in the <a href={href('skills/')}>skilltree planner</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="guide-topic" id="combat" aria-labelledby="combat-title">
      <header class="guide-heading">
        <QuestIcon name="steel_sword" size={28} />
        <h2 id="combat-title">Practice with your first weapon</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="guide-body">
        <p>Check your weapon’s grip and moveset in the <a href={href('weapons/')}>weapon registry</a>. Try regular, sprinting and aerial attacks on safe terrain so you know their reach before taking on a dungeon.</p>
        <p>The <a href={href('guides/tutorial/#combat')}>combat tutorial</a> covers Epic Fight movement, dodging and automatic combat switching.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<script>
  const movedGuides: Record<string, string> = {
    '#walking-machines': 'guides/walking-machines/',
    '#workshop-builds': 'tutorials/#workshop-builds',
  };

  function followMovedGuide() {
    const destination = movedGuides[location.hash];
    if (destination) location.replace(import.meta.env.BASE_URL + destination);
  }

  window.addEventListener('hashchange', followMovedGuide);
  followMovedGuide();
</script>

<style>
  .guide-jumps {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0 20px;
    margin: 0 0 24px;
  }
  .guide-jumps a {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 44px;
    font-size: 15px;
    font-weight: 550;
  }
  .guide-topics { display: grid; gap: 20px; }
  .guide-topic {
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  .guide-heading {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    min-height: 60px;
    padding: 12px 18px;
    background: linear-gradient(#211813c9, #211813df), var(--guide-spruce) 0 0 / 48px 48px repeat;
    color: #fff4e8;
  }
  .guide-heading h2 { margin: 0; font-size: clamp(18px, 2.1vw, 23px); line-height: 1.2; }
  .guide-body { padding: 18px; color: var(--muted); }
  .guide-body > *:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .guide-body strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 620; }
  .guide-body ol, .guide-body ul { margin: 0 0 16px; }
  .guide-body li { padding-inline-start: 3px; }
  .guide-figure { margin: 16px 0; }
  .guide-figure:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .guide-figure img { display: block; max-width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 5px; }
  .guide-figure figcaption { margin-top: 6px; color: var(--subtle); font-size: 14px; }
  .material-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .material {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-soft);
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: var(--bg);
  }
  .material img { flex-shrink: 0; border-radius: 2px; image-rendering: pixelated; }
  .material h3 { margin: 0; color: var(--text); font-size: 16px; }
  .material p { margin: 3px 0 0; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.5; }
  .identifier-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto; align-items: start; gap: 16px; }
  .identifier-layout > div > :last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .identifier-layout img { display: block; width: 144px; height: auto; }

  @media (max-width: 635px) {
    .guide-body, .guide-heading { padding-inline: 14px; }
    .material-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .identifier-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 6px; }
    .identifier-layout img { grid-row: 1; width: 112px; }
  }
</style>
